BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Rollcrate) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary: Rollcrate) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Every semester, millions of college students move into and out of dorms. Most of them use) Tj T* (whatever is cheap and available, like cardboard boxes, plastic bins, trash bags, and laundry) Tj T* (baskets. These options are not great. Cardboard boxes tear and get soggy, plastic bins are) Tj T* (bulky and hard to carry, and bags do not protect anything fragile. Students also have to carry) Tj T* (heavy loads across parking lots, up stairs, and through crowded hallways, which is tiring and) Tj T* (sometimes causes injuries. At the end of the year, many of these containers get thrown away,) Tj T* (which is wasteful, and then students have to buy new ones the next fall.) Tj T* () Tj T* (A second problem is storage. Many students who live far from campus or study abroad need) Tj T* (somewhere to keep their belongings over the summer. Storage companies and campus storage) Tj T* (programs charge fees that can add up to a few hundred dollars a year, and students often feel) Tj T* (they have no choice but to pay.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Rollcrate is a foldable storage crate with built-in wheels and a telescoping pull handle. When) Tj T* (it is unfolded, it is a sturdy container that holds a large amount of clothing, books, bedding,) Tj T* (and small electronics. When it is folded, it collapses to roughly the thickness of a textbook) Tj T* (so it can slide under a bed, behind a door, or into a closet. The crate is made from a durable) Tj T* (fabric-and-polymer material that is water resistant and designed to last for several years.) Tj T* (Because it is reusable, students do not need to buy new boxes each year.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We believe Rollcrate also helps students save on storage. Because the crate is easy to pack,) Tj T* (label, and stack, students can use cheaper options like a friend's garage or a shared unit, and) Tj T* (some campuses may let students keep crates in their own storage rooms at reduced cost.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are about nineteen million college students in the United States, and a large share of) Tj T* (them live on campus at some point. Our target is first and second year students who live in) Tj T* (dorms and their parents, who often pay for the supplies. We estimate that about eight million) Tj T* (students live in campus housing each year. If each of them spent forty dollars on a moving and) Tj T* (storage product, that would be a market of around three hundred twenty million dollars. We) Tj T* (think this is a reasonable estimate, though it is based on general assumptions rather than) Tj T* (detailed research. Our first goal is to reach a small portion of this market, starting with) Tj T* (schools near our own university and expanding to other regions.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to sell Rollcrate directly to students and parents through our website, with prices) Tj T* (around thirty-five to forty-five dollars per crate and discounts for bundles of two or four. We) Tj T* (also plan to sell through campus bookstores and through back-to-school promotions that connect) Tj T* (with housing offices. A second revenue idea is to sell sponsored crates to universities and) Tj T* (housing departments, which could give them to incoming students with a school logo on them. Our) Tj T* (cost to make each crate is currently about eighteen dollars on a small production run, and we) Tj T* (expect this to drop with larger orders. We have not yet tested all of these channels, and our) Tj T* (pricing may change as we learn more from customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The space for dorm and moving products is crowded. There are many existing options, including) Tj T* (plastic bins, rolling carts, collapsible crates, duffel bags with wheels, and large retail kits) Tj T* (sold each August by big-box stores and online marketplaces. Some of these products are cheap,) Tj T* (and some are well known. Our view is that none of them combines folding, wheels, and durability) Tj ET
endstream
