BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (in a single product that is designed specifically for the dorm move. Still, we know that larger) Tj T* (companies could copy our idea, and that students are often price sensitive and may just choose) Tj T* (the cheapest thing available. Our advantage is that we are focused on one customer and can move) Tj T* (quickly, but we do not yet have a patent or strong brand.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marcus Delacroix-Ibarra is our CEO and handles overall strategy, customer conversations, and) Tj T* (sales. He is a junior studying business and has experience working in a campus retail job.) Tj T* (Priya Venkataraghavan leads product design and is a mechanical engineering student who built) Tj T* (the first prototypes and manages relationships with our manufacturing contact. Tobias) Tj T* (Ellingsworth is responsible for marketing and our website, and has experience running social) Tj T* (media for a student club. Naomi Achterberg manages finances and operations, including our LLC) Tj T* (paperwork and order tracking. We all attend our university and work on Rollcrate part time) Tj T* (alongside classes.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined our core concept, registered Rollcrate as an LLC, built a working) Tj T* (prototype, and launched a website. We gave early versions of the crate to a small number of) Tj T* (students who tried them during a move-in weekend and gave us feedback, which was mostly) Tj T* (positive, although some said the handle felt loose. We have also received our first payment) Tj T* (from a customer, who purchased a set of crates through our website. Revenue to date is small,) Tj T* (under a few hundred dollars. Our spending so far has come from the founders' own savings and a) Tj T* (small amount of money from family, totaling about four thousand dollars, mostly for prototypes,) Tj T* (the website, and legal filing fees.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Over the next twelve months, we plan to complete a first production run of about five hundred) Tj T* (crates, improve the handle design, and sell mainly during the fall move-in season. We project) Tj T* (revenue of roughly fifteen to twenty thousand dollars in the first year if sales go as planned,) Tj T* (but this is a rough estimate and depends on how well our marketing works. We expect to be near) Tj T* (break-even after the first production run and to need additional funds to grow beyond that.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to this competition to win funding and to gain mentorship. We are hoping for a) Tj T* (prize of around ten thousand dollars, which we would use mainly to pay for our first production) Tj T* (run and to improve the product based on feedback. Beyond funding, we would value guidance from) Tj T* (judges and advisors on pricing, how to approach university housing offices, and how to protect) Tj T* (our design. We would also like introductions to manufacturers and to anyone with experience) Tj T* (selling consumer products to students. We believe Rollcrate can make moving easier and cheaper) Tj T* (for students, and we are excited to keep building it.) Tj ET
